      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO AGRICULTURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Farming in India is categorized into Subsistence Farming, Commercial Farming, and Plantation Farming.",
        "Agricultural activities are structured around three main cropping seasons: Kharif, Rabi, and Zaid.",
        "Critical historical interventions include Irrigation developments, the Green Revolution, and Land Reforms.",
        "Current emphasis centers on Agricultural Marketing, Government Initiatives, and resolving systemic challenges to shape the future of Indian agriculture."
